## Secrets & security (non-negotiable)

- Secrets come from <.env / user-secrets / vault>. **Never** read, print, or commit them; never hardcode a secret in code, tests, or docs.
- <List secret-holding paths agents must never touch.>
- Every new endpoint needs: an explicit authorization decision, validation on all input, and error responses that leak no internals.
- All data access parameterized — no string-interpolated SQL, ever.

## Definition of done — every change, before you call it finished

1. Build clean — zero *new* warnings introduced.
2. Tests all green (same command as CI). New behavior has new tests.
3. Format check clean (same commands as CI).
4. New/changed endpoints pass the security checklist (see `.claude/skills/security-checklist/`).
5. Work on a feature branch, never directly on `main`. Small, reviewable commits.

